    Replaces the Command::spawn() path on Windows with the full broker

    (spawn_sandboxed). The broker integrates ALL four sandbox layers:

    C1 (Job Object kill-on-close + memory limit), C2 (restricted token via

    CreateProcessAsUserW + CreateRestrictedToken(DISABLE_MAX_PRIVILEGE)),

    C3 (filesystem ACLs via icacls), C4 (network block via netsh advfirewall).

    run_windows() method: spawns via spawn_sandboxed, takes pipe HANDLEs and

    converts to std::fs::File via FromRawHandle, drains stdout/stderr in

    threads (same drain_capped as Unix path), uses SandboxedChild::try_wait

    + kill for the timeout wait loop, calls wait_and_restore() at the end

    (which restores ACLs + removes firewall rule + closes handles via Drop).

    The macOS/Linux path (Command::spawn + Seatbelt + rlimits) is unchanged.

    The previous C3+C4 shortcut code (apply before Command::spawn) is removed

    because the broker handles everything internally.

